# `go build ./...` in the PARENT module writes nothing, because it matches several packages and the
# toolchain then compiles as a check and discards the objects - the module's pom says so at length.
# THIS directory is one `main` package, so the same command DOES write a binary here, named after
# the directory. run.sh and the Dockerfile both use `go build -o` and put theirs in target/; this
# catches the one a developer produces by hand.
/demo
